b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Although I'm almost certain that it won't be a V5 publication.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to derail the discussion but V5 storyteller vault is really what the line needs right now, it's getting kinda stagnant imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:14:23-08:00","id":1422023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422016#post1422016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just out of curiosity and with no disrespect: Is being a witch in real life an american thing? And is this a thing along the line of religious belief or more like when people had the Jedi religion or the flying spaghetti monster thing? (You know, like something that works like a religion on a phenomenal level but is not taken seriously on an existential basis.)<br /> <br /> I don't want to derail the thread, but I was seriously curious (because with VtM being a predominantly american product sometimes it's nice to see the underlying world view of the authors in order to estimate which parts you keep and which parts you cross out when planning a chronicle in europe).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's a real religion.<br /> <br /> Neo-Paganism isn't something I ascribe to but quite a lot of people take incredibly seriously in both America as well as Britain.<br /> <br /> Non-Wicca variants exist in other parts of Europe as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:26:34-08:00","id":1422025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422023#post1422023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's a real religion.<br /> <br /> Neo-Paganism isn't something I ascribe to but quite a lot of people take incredibly seriously in both America as well as Britain.<br /> <br /> Non-Wicca variants exist in other parts of Europe as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, thanks. I knew that there was a paganist revival during approx. the last twenty years in europe but here it was always &lt;1% of people and almost always with no existential commitment and more along the lines of aesthetics. So thanks again for the insight.<br /> <br /> That could possibly lead to interesting consequences for demographics of european Tremere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422017#post1422017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to derail the discussion but V5 storyteller vault is really what the line needs right now, it's getting kinda stagnant imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really like that. But up until now there is literally not a single ST vault publication for V5, is it? Is there a specific reason for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:29:21-08:00","id":1422027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422025#post1422025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would really like that. But up until now there is literally not a single ST vault publication for V5, is it? Is there a specific reason for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The powers that be haven't opened it up for creation yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:33:42-08:00","id":1422030,"title":"","content":"Neo-pagans exist across europe. But I'm not sure as to how many take it seriously and how many are just having fun larping or 'getting in touch with their culture'.<br /> <br /> Historical Real life witchcraft was more about poisoning your neighbours dog , saying aloud the very bad things you want to happen to someone, not being all that religious, and in general being a very unpopular person. Poisonings were the cause of a lot of witch killings. Some very bored people with not enough to do started writing very spicy books that got a lot of attention and later on some competing forms of Christianity might have gotten a little too excited over the prospect of killing witches to prove the efficacy of their faith over other branches (It added variety to burned heretics). Killing witches for the most part was far less common than you'd think, and far too many like to point at it as religious madness<br /> <br /> At some point witch hunts caught on in the new world despite the lack of religious conflict because... You've seen what Americans are like, right? Those puritans were England's crazy rejects.<br /> <br /> Modern real life witchcraft is inspired by movies inspired by other movies who looked at those fancy books some very creative men wrote back in the day, practiced by women who don't fit in all that well (just like the historic lot) and need a sense of belonging. So they form friendship groups and adopt strange fashions and stuff, and then they get some feminist wicca stuff in there because it sounds nice and the stuff that those men with too much time on their hands wrote is more than a little mean to women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:21:20-08:00","id":1422061,"title":"","content":"All that said I don't think modern 'witches' will be well suited to unlife as warlocks in anything resembling an efficient and pragmatic magical organization that can reasonably politic with vampires. I had a short rant with some really out-there analogues, but it's all-too easy to get nasty. Point being, Thaumaturges, no matter their style (Hermetic, Heaven and earth, Settite clerical high magic, Punk magic) Need <b>exceptional</b> intelligence, Willpower, a well rounded belief system, and a strong commitment to goals. If you yourself are a Tremere, You are unlikely to find all of these qualities among Idealists who aspire to be Hollywood witches, people embracing a fad, or folks needing a support group. These people make for great Herd dots, but rarely vampires, and even rarer thaumaturges. Even when you do find such people, you are not likely to find many, it's probable that they don't play well with others, and in any case it's highly unlikely that you'll be able to make an organization that can rival the Real Tremere.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy is hard and requires sacrifice. It's not meant to be for everyone. Would you be happy if necromancers could distance themselves from the dead and still practice their arts? <br /> <br /> Now, the interesting thing, is that I kinda like the Idea of House Carna.<br /> But that's working under the assumption that this harmful new-wave feminist stereotype they've got going on is really just a facade to distance themselves from the Tremere, and really they're Hermetic Tremere Group B in secret and perhaps the whole plan is to use different Tremere brands to get a chantry into every single city, especially with cities that have historically been hostile to the Tremere brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-05-2020, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:27:25-08:00","id":1422065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422061#post1422061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's working under the assumption that this harmful new-wave feminist stereotype they've got going on is really just a facade to distance themselves from the Tremere, and really they're Hermetic Tremere Group B in secret and perhaps the whole plan is to use different Tremere brands to get a chantry into every single city, especially with cities that have historically been hostile to the Tremere brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I can get behind, otherwise just give them Cr\u00faac and call it what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 11-05-2020, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:45:00-08:00","id":1422069,"title":"","content":"Bahari<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga<br /> <br /> Kolduns<br /> <br /> Nature witchery is nothing new in V:TM.<br /> <br /> And as we know, Tzimisce have always been superior to the Usurpers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B