The Tzmisce got bodied left and right by the Tremere. Don't know where you're getting the idea that they're better from. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm genuinely confused.<br /> <br /> What exactly is progressive?<br /> <br /> Carna is a witch because it's magic that's thousands of years old. She's a ruthless evil vampire Elder. It's just she's freed herself from the Elders above her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422077#post1422077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's probably an old path, lifted from perhaps OG pagans, Dur-An-Ki, or Setite sorcery if not conceived independently by the Hermetics themselves during the times in which cities were small and the wilderness dominated.<br /> <br /> Edit: Nature paths are not the sole domain of progressive hippies goddammit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Carna was Embraced in 1419 and was the Prince of Marseilles.<br /> <br /> What, exactly, is progressive about her other than she Embraces feminine magic and freedom for her fellow Tremere?<br /> <br /> Lucita was also an Elder antagonist to her sire. For her own benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-05-2020, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T12:12:53-08:00","id":1422097,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of House Carna. It provides more options and diversity, basically the opposite of what happened with the Hecate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T12:52:32-08:00","id":1422102,"title":"","content":"Are you genuinely confused? Or do you know exactly what I mean and have decided you don't like my precise choice of words?<br /> <br /> Tzmisce, especially Kolduns, are infamously <b>conservative</b>. Their magic is as traditional as it gets, and their sire-child relationships are strict. Above all, be they shapers or wizards, Tzmisce value intelligence.<br /> They're not going to take in soothsayers, wiccans, people who practice 'feminine magics' or who like the idea of 'freedom' as you imagine it. People like that don't make good Tzmisce, nor Tremere, nor do they make good ashipu, or priests. Shit I doubt Bahari of all people want the kind of people you seem so desperate to include. These people might pop up as independent thaumaturges, but they're not going to be all that good. Remember; there's a little rule in V20 at least that suggests you need at least 3 dots of Occult if you're going to actually use magic that hasn't been drilled into you by a tutor and magic isn't an inate part of your blood. Do you actually think these people are going to have those three dots of Occult? I mean, three dots of occult in relation to magic, not into UFOs. I'm sure you can strike gold and find the right person from one of these groups, but how likely is that, and can you fill a chantry with them?<br /> <br /> Look, I get your desire, your want, to make magic more inclusive. From an out-of-character perspective, you're half justified. But it's not right in character, you need to know it's your headcanon, and insisting that a legitimately open-to-mystic-nonsense House Carna would have chantries anywhere with knowledge equal to an apprenticeship of two Assamite sorcerers and their stockpile of magic hash is laughable, let alone the Gold standard of Tremere chantries. The psychology is against you. The sociology is against you. The metaphysics of the WoD are against you. Any knowledge of how business organization works would tell you that House Carna, if we take their description in v5 at face value, would not work well in any market that's competitive.<br /> <br /> When I make a Ventrue character, I don't make them uncouth with working class values. I don't make Ventrue without social skills. I don't need to. I don't need my Ventrue character to have my skills or my values. I'm happy with making a Ventrue with Ventrue values; perhaps I'll spice them up with some off-ventrue thinking, but at the end of character creation I'l have a Ventrue of clan Ventrue. Imagine the shock and horror it would cause if suddenly half the Ventrue became insufferable hobos who wanted Anarcho-socialism?<br /> <br /> Why then, is there a group of Tremere who fundamentally break the rules of being a Tremere? Why is that Ok? The first rule of Thaumaturgy is that it takes a lot of effort. But now there are next to no standards and anyone can do it and be part of an effective organization. Imagine how much that sucks to people who've actually put effort into it?<br /> <br /> You like malkavians <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> . The prospect of losing my mind scares the shit out of me IRL. What If, to accommodate people like myself more, V6 came out and said that now half the Malkavians are now completely sane, and instead... their weakness is that they know they're in a tabletop game and they get upset if the storyteller declares the difficulty's pretty high for the dice pool they've got? Oh and maybe dominate isn't that nasty anymore and only makes you a little more persuasive rather than forcing people to act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-05-2020, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T13:02:55-08:00","id":1422104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422102#post1422102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you genuinely confused? Or do you know exactly what I mean and have decided you don't like my precise choice of words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument makes no sense because in what universe is Carna PROGRESSIVE?<br /> <br /> She is a reactionary throw back embracing millennia old ancient magics and atavistic blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> And does so with the help of the f***ing Necronomicon.<br /> <br /> Yes, she has women in her service and believes they were oppressed under the old system. However, the Verbena are about TEN THOUSAND years older as a tradition than the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> Its elitist and exclusive, it's just a different kind of exclusion. They're not hippies and I've said this like 5 or 6 times but you keep acting like they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why then, is there a group of Tremere who fundamentally break the rules of being a Tremere? Why is that Ok? The first rule of Thaumaturgy is that it takes a lot of effort. But now there are next to no standards and anyone can do it and be part of an effective organization. Imagine how much that sucks to people who've actually put effort into it? </div> </div> </div>Do I need to point out that you've just made this up about House Carna? Why do you believe that they aren't MORE restrictive than the Tremere? A Tremere who can't get with the ancient forces is worthless and a lot of Modern Tremere materialists simply will not past muster in House carna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-05-2020, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T13:34:53-08:00","id":1422106,"title":"","content":"Forget Carna herself for a moment. I'm talking about the people she recruits and her sales pitch. Do you recall her sales pitch? That little bit where three Tremere meet up and they represent the three houses? She wants to recruit people who 'love magic for it's own sake' IE <i>fucking amateurs. </i><br /> <br /> And look, being elitist when you exclusively recruit from wicca types... Are we playing vampire miracle workers or housewives with a sense of identity? Reverse-elitism does not make for good embrace choices, at least for mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T14:42:56-08:00","id":1422119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote