on which book you are looking at, both in the real world and in terms of when things are set in the WoD. Some of the material has Tremere the wizard leaving his body and taking possession of Goratrix as far back as when Goratrix was recalled to Ceoris in the 13th century, and some of it has Tremere the wizard taking possession in the 1990s. This puts the narrative of Blood Treachery into question. But the idea of Tremere sometimes physically turning into a giant maggot grub thing (after diablerizing Saulot) goes all the way back to the 1st edition book Children of the Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T06:19:57-08:00","id":1422234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422233#post1422233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This depends on which book you are looking at, both in the real world and in terms of when things are set in the WoD. Some of the material has Tremere the wizard leaving his body and taking possession of Goratrix as far back as when Goratrix was recalled to Ceoris in the 13th century, and some of it has Tremere the wizard taking possession in the 1990s. This puts the narrative of Blood Treachery into question. But the idea of Tremere sometimes physically turning into a giant maggot grub thing (after diablerizing Saulot) goes all the way back to the 1st edition book Children of the Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand correct, GRR.<br /> <br /> My Vampire: The Masquerade Lore skill is 4 versus your 5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T06:30:43-08:00","id":1422236,"title":"","content":"Feh. I might be <i>wrong </i>- I will need to reread the Etrius section from CotI.<br /> <br /> Edit: I was wrong. CotI does not mention this but does say Etrius thought it was a bad idea. The idea Tremere himself has been replaced by something else, possibly a giant white worm, appeared in the 1st edition Clan Tremere book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 11-06-2020, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T11:23:54-08:00","id":1422455,"title":"","content":"Just to toss my own two cents out.<br /> <br /> I generally use House Carna as inspiration for my own thing, as I\u2019ve mentioned as my general philosophy before.<br /> <br /> Clan Tremere has always had its problems. Elder vampires often graduate out of more biological discernment\u2019s because of alienation and practicality... but they also get calcified in their values and beliefs. I have no doubt that there were inroads to power for those who fell outside House Tremere\u2019s identity norm, but it had the same tensions and difficulties of any other old boys club, and that\u2019s certainly what the Hermetics and House Tremere was and to an extent still is.<br /> <br /> Yet I don\u2019t think that\u2019s the main issue for the clan schism. It\u2019s certainly a factor, particularly amongst ancillae and younger kindred who feel unfairly disadvantaged on account of identity. However I feel the larger elements, the ones that cross generational and ideological lines, are the ones that most guaranteed a schism within the clan. The intense stratification, the intensely proscriptive orthodoxy, the intensely hierarchy\u2019s structure, the intensely rigid customs; the virtual impossibility of advancement for so many and the rampant infighting tacitly encouraged by superiors.<br /> <br /> House Tremere would be a nightmare to exist within, even if your thaumaturgical and political philosophy are perfectly in line with house orthodoxy. If you have interests which are unorthodox though, things were not so easy. This alongside the alienation and frustration the strict hierarchy guarantees, particularly amongst those whose blood bonds break, guarantees some level of inevitable dissent.<br /> <br /> I think House Carna is an excellent inspiration for manifesting that dissent within the narrative. I never liked the destruction of House Goratrix because I felt there needed to be a counter-weight to House Tremere. There needed to be some cracks in the Pyramid, it was inevitable in my opinion, and those Houses demonstrated the consequences of those cracks.<br /> <br /> Houses Carna &amp; Goratrix, in their own fashions, offered an escape to many. To the disadvantaged, ambitious, frustrated, and unorthodox; they could become very attractive alternatives to an eternity of service to the Pyramid.<br /> <br /> The ritual to break the blood bond is I think one of the most critical and interesting ideas that either antitribu house has and is foundational to their viability. I also think that their sect associations are invaluable though.<br /> <br /> House Goratrix would not have survived as long as it did without the Sabbat. Hell, House Tremere would not survive as long as it has without the Camarilla. The warlocks have enemies throughout the natural and supernatural world, even when they are able to unify their own houses into action. imo House Carna would need to establish a healthy relationship with the Anarch Movement in order to survive and presenting themselves as radical dissenters breaking away from the tyranny of the Pyramid is an excellent way to do so.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt that Carna is as ambitious, arrogant, and power-hungry as Tremere or Goratrix and I don\u2019t think she should be presented as particularly different from those two (outside of propaganda). She wants to maintain control over her own organization through different means however. She\u2019s willing to tolerate a loose union and non-collective structure of pseudo-independent cells and operations for the same reason that the Anarchs do: flexibility and resilience.<br /> <br /> House Tremere retains their supremacy in blood thaumaturgical but I think a critical part of keeping the warlocks interesting is ensuring the constant threat of risk. The independent clans shepherd their own blood sorceries and the Sabbat and Anarchs house alternative to the Camarilla\u2019s own warlocks.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this is a gambit from Tremere themself or perhaps this is a trick of Saulot; regardless I think the division of the Tremere is a valuable addition to the meta plot and I do thank V5 for inspiring it to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T11:32:12-08:00","id":1422457,"title":"","content":"One of the things that has been organically emerging in my game with the Tremere is the fact that each of the Houses have been coalescing into different <i>styles</i> of Blood Magic. They've been less about their political and social aims and more about simply what sort of sorcery the Tremere in question practices.<br /> <br /> <b>House Tremere</b>: Wizard Classic. The Tremere use wands, wear robes, have spellbooks, and are very much the Order of Hermes in 2020 as they were in 1220. They are not updated because what worked for them then works for them now.<br /> <br /> <b>House Carna</b>: They're doing the nature worship, sex magic, cauldrons, and athames. They're all classically trained witches and wizards but experimenting with more primeval stuff. Oddly, they don't necessarily know what they're channelling but are growing in power, nevertheless.<br /> <br /> <b>House Ipissmus</b>: I've been using these guys lately as the Tremere technocrats despite their Thelmic name. Guys with Silicon Valley laboratories, computers, bio-thaumaturgical experimentation, and more. They're the House Thig of the Tremere versus Carna's Diende.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T11:51:08-08:00","id":1422462,"title":"","content":"....Wands and Robes..? LOL","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T12:08:07-08:00","id":1422467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-d