re what revolution there is to be, the camarilla is pretty much done,<br /> just a matter of time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T12:41:05-08:00","id":1422811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422809#post1422809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ye, but Carna isn't part of the sabbat, she is part of the Camarilla,<br /> same for Lasombra who still hold the vaulderie<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what revolution there is to be, the camarilla is pretty much done,<br /> just a matter of time</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla has gained two new clans and lost its greatest enemies. It's also opened up diplomatic relations with the Ashirra and taken Japan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T21:09:30-08:00","id":1424452,"title":"","content":"House Carna is fine, their magical style is fine, and it's really weird to build up an extremely insulting and inaccurate view of modern pagan practices and then attribute them to a group of fictional vampires practicing literal blood magic in a fictional world with a vast array of working magical practices dating back thousands of years. And it's not inherently progressive for anyone to want women to have more leeway, more rights, etc. That's how it is in the modern world, but Carna didn't come at this from the perspective of second or third wave feminists. She came at it from the perspective that she didn't like how she was treated within the Pyramid. Like it or not, it's perfectly normal to not like mistreatment and want to change it.<br /> <br /> Also, Wicca and modern witchcraft aren't based on modern movies about witches. Look up Gerald Gardner. You don't have to agree with him, you don't have to think his scholarship is good, you don't even have to think Wicca is a valid religion, but you could at least understand that modern Wiccan and Witchcraft traditions are not actually based on Hollywood witches.<br /> <br /> V5's rendition of Carna's new age hippy Hollywood witchcraft:<br /> <br /> &quot;Carna always found this ritual unwholesome, but playing with blood was a dirty business. Calling on her vitae to give strength, she used a warm spoon to pop free the unconscious victim\u2019s eyeball. She sighed, quite humanlike, as she twisted the orb from its tether and placed it in her mouth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Holding her hand out, the eye still in place on her tongue, her clanmate placed a heavy knife on Carna\u2019s palm. Without hesitation, she pulled the tip of the victim\u2019s tongue out between his teeth, and sawed through the muscular organ. She placed the tip in her mouth, and proceeded to swallow the two components as her fellow Tremere treated the man\u2019s bleeding orifices.<br /> <br /> &quot;Carna turned to study the Thracian text on the wall overlooking this entire macabre scene. The man had resisted her mental compulsions, had refused to translate the work willingly, and would have never succumbed to torture. It was a sad necessity that she would have to take his eye and tongue to read and speak the ancient language known only to him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Real summer of love stuff.<br /> <br /> Yes, she's embracing modern occultists, but &quot;hippy new age hollywood witchcraft&quot; is not an accurate way to describe the entirety of modern occultism and magical practices, nor does it address the fact that they have to learn to use the blood magic regardless. Given that magic in general in the WoD is mutable depending upon the practitioner and their training, rejecting the validity of chaos magic, modern witchcraft, etc. is a parochial stance to take, and not one particularly well suited to the WoD. It's well-suited <i>in-character </i>to traditionalists like Schrekt, and that's actually really good - the clash of ancient and elder practices against modern, newer ones is actually a big part of the WoD in general and Vampire in specific. There's no particular reason why it couldn't happen to magical practice as much as it happens to say neonates vs. elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-17-2020, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T07:40:13-08:00","id":1424930,"title":"","content":"Edit: not worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 11-19-2020, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T15:39:40-08:00","id":1425028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1424452#post1424452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Carna always found this ritual unwholesome, but playing with blood was a dirty business. Calling on her vitae to give strength, she used a warm spoon to pop free the unconscious victim\u2019s eyeball. She sighed, quite humanlike, as she twisted the orb from its tether and placed it in her mouth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Holding her hand out, the eye still in place on her tongue, her clanmate placed a heavy knife on Carna\u2019s palm. Without hesitation, she pulled the tip of the victim\u2019s tongue out between his teeth, and sawed through the muscular organ. She placed the tip in her mouth, and proceeded to swallow the two components as her fellow Tremere treated the man\u2019s bleeding orifices.<br /> <br /> &quot;Carna turned to study the Thracian text on the wall overlooking this entire macabre scene. The man had resisted her mental compulsions, had refused to translate the work willingly, and would have never succumbed to torture. It was a sad necessity that she would have to take his eye and tongue to read and speak the ancient language known only to him.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a Tremere ritual, Eyes of Babel, from V20 Rites of Blood. I want to say it may have appeared in other books, too. So it's not unique to Carna's style.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm against house Carna or adding more styles, nor do I particularly care if they incorporate Wicca, hollywood witchcraft or inspiration from real old school paganism. I still find the injection of variety and options interesting rather than them all practicing the same style. I mean look at the Hollow Ones, they incorporate all kinds of random stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T15:43:27-08:00","id":1425029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425028#post1425028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a Tremere ritual, Eyes of Babel, from V20 Rites of Blood. I want to say it may have appeared in other books, too. So it's not unique to Carna's style.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm against house Carna or adding more styles, nor do I particularly care if they incorporate Wicca, hollywood witchcraft or inspiration from real old school paganism. I still find the injection of variety and options interesting rather than them all practicing the same style. I mean look at the Hollow Ones, they incorporate all kinds of random stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. More styles are good.<br /> <br /> My point wasn't that it was strictly Carna's style, but more the idea that House Carna does some kind of new agey sweetness and light version of blood magic was nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T15:53:58-08:00","id":1425032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425029#post1425029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I agree. More styles are good.<br /> <br /> My point wasn't that it was strictly Carna's style, but more the idea that House Carna does some kind of new agey sweetness and light version of blood magic was nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're vampires and blood witches.<br /> <br /> Which is something that V:TM has had forever but was never nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">