cussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425032#post1425032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're vampires and blood witches.<br /> <br /> Which is something that V:TM has had forever but was never nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:18:00-08:00","id":1425039,"title":"","content":"The odd fact about the complaint here is that it was one that was addressed in another line as early as 1st Edition Mage: The Ascension. One of the things about their Tradition Book was the fact that the Verbena REALLY DISLIKE New Agers. A lot of their training is designed to beat the happy, sanitized Walt Disney version of paganism out of the heads of their followers and instill a dark, bloody, Lilith worshiping World of Darkness witchcraft in their heads.<br /> <br /> Human sacrifice, Isle 8, monstrous curses, Isle 9.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:19:43-08:00","id":1425041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425039#post1425039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odd fact about the complaint here is that it was one that was addressed in another line as early as 1st Edition Mage: The Ascension. One of the things about their Tradition Book was the fact that the Verbena REALLY DISLIKE New Agers. A lot of their training is designed to beat the happy, sanitized Walt Disney version of paganism out of the heads of their followers and instill a dark, bloody, Lilith worshiping World of Darkness witchcraft in their heads.<br /> <br /> Human sacrifice, Isle 8, monstrous curses, Isle 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they got brought into the fold come revised","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:24:52-08:00","id":1425046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425041#post1425041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except they got brought into the fold come revised</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't a big fan of some changes done to the Revised Traditions, I admit.<br /> <br /> What? Me? Old School!<br /> <br /> Never!<br /> <br /> I drifted out of Mage when the Technocracy stopped being fascists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:32:42-08:00","id":1425049,"title":"","content":"Finding OG witches suitable for unlife is gonna be really hard in our modern world. It would be totally unreasonable to assume HC could find enough neonates in their city to form a chantry. But also it's a lot harder for them to embrace a promising person who would then be interested and capable of drawing from... what paradigm do they use again? The Hermetic stuff is pretty palatable to a newcomer. Paganism? far less so. <br /> <br /> and, y'know, a good chunk of the doylist reasoning for house carna is that they wanted magic characters to be easy and accessible to anyone. The other half is of doylist reasoning would be every conservative faction needs to be a Heel for a more... what's a term i can use that won't be nitpicked... neoliberal Face? <br /> <br /> point being. most players who pick HC over HT are going to be... well, less interested in playing the domineering arogant types Tremere are known for. Less OG paganism, more holywood: even if house Carna is supposed to be just as mean as HT, it caters towards players who aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:40:57-08:00","id":1425052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425049#post1425049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finding OG witches suitable for unlife is gonna be really hard in our modern world. It would be totally unreasonable to assume HC could find enough neonates in their city to form a chantry. But also it's a lot harder for them to embrace a promising person who would then be interested and capable of drawing from... what paradigm do they use again? The Hermetic stuff is pretty palatable to a newcomer. Paganism? far less so.<br /> <br /> and, y'know, a good chunk of the doylist reasoning for house carna is that they wanted magic characters to be easy and accessible to anyone. The other half is of doylist reasoning would be every conservative faction needs to be a Heel for a more... what's a term i can use that won't be nitpicked... neoliberal Face?<br /> <br /> point being. most players who pick HC over HT are going to be... well, less interested in playing the domineering arogant types Tremere are known for. Less OG paganism, more holywood: even if house Carna is supposed to be just as mean as HT, it caters towards players who aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Just grab some people and train them.<br /> <br /> How do the Bahari recruit people?<br /> <br /> Or Tzimisce?<br /> <br /> Or hell, the Sabbat as a whole.<br /> <br /> You brainwash them to join your sick murder cult. Which is what any vampire religion will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:41:10-08:00","id":1425053,"title":"","content":"&quot;The founder of this house twisted off a guy's eye and cut out his tongue in the flavor text. This inspires me to play Prue from Charmed!&quot; no one said ever.<br /> <br /> Some other stuff:<br /> <br /> Hedge magic is a thing in the WoD, especially thanks to &quot;mythic threads&quot; per revised or whatever people want to call them otherwise.<br /> Getting involved in modern paganism does not in fact preclude someone from having some magical ability<br /> Not all modern paganism is &quot;new age&quot; or &quot;hollywood witches&quot;<br /> Modern pagans are able to discern the difference between practicing a real world religion and modeling mysticism off The Craft or something, and tend to find the latter fun but not actually a signpost to actual practice<br /> If anyone can tell if someone's a practitioner, struggling but with potential, or doesn't have potential at all, it'd be a blood magic practitioner deciding who to Embrace to bring into House Carna.<br /> I tend to think modern paganism in the WoD is going to at least have a bias toward actual functional practice, even if the majority can't do it.<br /> <br /> Headcanon House Carna as new age Willow Rosenbergs all you want, but I don't think the text supports that in the slightest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-19-2020, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:43:54-08:00","id":1425055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425052#post1425052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. Just grab some people and train them.<br /> <br /> How do the Bahari recruit people?<br /> <br /> Or Tzimisce?<br /> <br /> Or hell, the Sabbat as a whole.<br /> <br /> You brainwash them to join your sick murder cult. Which is what any vampire religion will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of these folk are in the Camarilla, where there are standards. HC are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:47:20-08:00","id":1425057,"title":"","content":"The Ventrue are the leaders of the Camarilla and they beat their philosophy and etiquette into their childer with years of training, mental domination, and every other tool available. Same with House Tremere who add a communal blood bond to the mix for them. <br /> <br /> I personally prefer House Carna as an Anarch thing although I suppose a domain could decide to back Carna over Tremere, but either way, indoctrination is just as much apart of the Camarilla as any other vampiric sect. The Camarilla isn\u2019t exactly the easiest thing for a well-adjusted human to adapt to either so saying that House Carna is so particularly egregious just feels obtuse to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:48:29-08:00","id":1425058,"title":"","content":"The flavor text in V5 shows that House Carna is part of the greater Clan Tremere, even if not Schrekt's House Tremere itself. Carna herself has been in the Camarilla for centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:52:01-08:00","id":1425060,"title":"","content":"Aye, which is fair, just not how I personally like to go about things. But we ain\u2019t here to talk about my table so thank ya for throwing this out there, as I honestly don\u2019t actually keep up with V5 much except from the broad scale stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:54:24-08:00","id":1425061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425055#post1425055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of these folk are in the Camarilla, where there are standards. HC are.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 says the Camarilla is riddled with Blood Cults that do the exact same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1425058#post1425058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flavor text in V5 shows that House Carna is part of the greater Clan Tremere, even if not Schrekt's House Tremere itself. Carna herself has been in the Camarilla for centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, she's the former Prince of Marsailles and a serial killer.<br /> <br /> It probably drives Karl insane she's undoubtedly set up her own alternative magical options with the Camarilla. Worse, that they have to work together against the Assamites.<br /> <br /> She WAS defecting to the Anarchs but apparently stopped when she realized House Tremere was in no position to go after her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-19-2020, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:49:37-07:00","id":1446843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422164#post1422164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;OH MY GOD, SAULOT IS EVIL AND THIS IS ALL PART OF HIS MASTER PLAN&quot; thing was introduced by the Transylvania Chronicles with the big climax being Tremere being cast out of his body and forced to destroy the Antitribu in a mass ritual in order to stay competitive.<br /> <br /> So, 1998, assuming they had the whole thing planned out.<br /> <br /> Which is to say not EARLY in the line's run but certainly not late either.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Notably, Saulot being evil was so controversial they made the White Worm's identity ambiguous. But the Tremere Inner Council being subverted and the Antedeluvian being taken over was Pre-Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a little more complicated. Saulot as evil mastermind is indeed a Transylvania Chronicles thing - but Tremere in its torpor periods going through weird physical changes and possibly mutating into <i>something </i>has been around since their first clanbook, maybe even a little before even.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: just noticed GRR beat me to it a bunch of pages ago. That's what i get for posting without reading the whole thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1422457#post1422457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that has been organically emerging in my game with the Tremere is the fact that each of the Houses have been coalescing into different <i>styles</i> of Blood Magic. They've been less about their political and social aims and more about simply what sort of sorcery the Tremere in question practices.<br /> <br /> <b>House Tremere</b>: Wizard Classic. The Tremere use wands, wear robes, have spellbooks, and are very much the Order of Hermes in 2020 as they were in 1220. They are not updated because what worked for them then works for them now.<br /> <br /> <b>House Carna</b>: They're doing the nature worship, sex magic, cauldrons, and athames. They're all classically trained witches and wizards but experimenting with more primeval stuff. Oddly, they don't necessarily know what they're channelling but are growing in power, nevertheless.<br /> <br /> <b>House Ipissmus</b>: I've been using these guys lately as the Tremere technocrats despite their Thelmic name. Guys with Silicon Valley laboratories, computers, bio-thaumaturgical experimentation, and more. They're the House Thig of the Tremere versus Carna's Diende.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be completely honest, i still have to define a clear image of House Carna in my head, as while i kind of like the idea of a bunch of resentful Tremere ladies playing &quot;Wicca/Verbena gone Wild&quot;, it doesn't quite fit with my image of Carna as serial black widow (and possible diablerist), at least not yet, but then i'm the first to admit i have barely dipped my toes into V5 lore.<br /> <br /> <br /> About House Ipsissimus.... Doesn't Cult of the Blood Gods mention <b><i>Mortius </i></b>as a member of the house? He definitely doesn't fit with that &quot;technocratic magic-dipping mages&quot; image you're painting, at least to me. Guess i'll keep to the Thelemic in my own take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-01-2021, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T07:48:58-07:00","id":1447403,"title":"","content":"My issue with House Carna is they're...completely, absolutely, top to bottom, unnecessary. There was already a Tremere faction in the game, and had been for twenty years, that fit every desired meta-narrative check-box to a T, which had a <i>far</i> more compelling backstory and fit better into the metaplot: the Telyavs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T08:29:09-07:00","id":1447406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447403#post1447403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with House Carna is they're...completely, absolutely, top to bottom, unnecessary. There was already a Tremere faction in the game, and had been for twenty years, that fit every desired meta-narrative check-box to a T, which had a <i>far</i> more compelling backstory and fit better into the metaplot: the Telyavs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There can't be both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-04-2021, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T08:53:46-07:00","id":1447409,"title":"","content":"The fans and the market determine what is needed and more gamers - i.e people buying books - seem interested in House Carna than are interested in the Telyavs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:07:25-07:00","id":1447430,"title":"","content":"If you want to go for a meta perspective and decide you want to attract people of the &quot;House Carna&quot; vibe, it'd be far less damaging to put emphasis on Anarch/Bahari groups that are intent on sharing occult secrets and forming witch circles and the like. HC as a house hurts the Tremere clan, not by being opposition, but by not taking things as seriously as the Tremere clan and yet still being treated as a viable option.. The Tremere pour their hearts and souls into magic, they invest themselves into a religious paradigm, and their organizational structure is optimized for this. Yet HC implies that friendship circles and people who pay undue attention to internet horoscopes are -equal-. Either give us an underdog story or come straight out and say it's a PR scam to get Tremere chantries into Tremere-hostile territories. Freelance sorcerers, cults, and OldSkhool sorcerers would give the &quot;HC&quot; types what they want without undermining the Tremere in such an unbelievable fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:55:20-07:00","id":1447469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447430#post1447430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to go for a meta perspective and decide you want to attract people of the &quot;House Carna&quot; vibe, it'd be far less damaging to put emphasis on Anarch/Bahari groups that are intent on sharing occult secrets and forming witch circles and the like. HC as a house hurts the Tremere clan, not by being opposition, but by not taking things as seriously as the Tremere clan and yet still being treated as a viable option.. The Tremere pour their hearts and souls into magic, they invest themselves into a religious paradigm, and their organizational structure is optimized for this. Yet HC implies that friendship circles and people who pay undue attention to internet horoscopes are -equal-. Either give us an underdog story or come straight out and say it's a PR scam to get Tremere chantries into Tremere-hostile territories. Freelance sorcerers, cults, and OldSkhool sorcerers would give the &quot;HC&quot; types what they want without undermining the Tremere in such an unbelievable fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you are a member of the Order of Hermes in RL roleplaying as a vampire somedays, MWIS.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Verbena paradigm is inferior!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:57:36-07:00","id":1447545,"title":"","content":"I'm not, nor have been a member of any such orders <br /> <br /> NGL Verbenna are one of the weaker ones, while Hermetics have one of the stronger paradigms. Hermetics are relatively inclusive and pro-establishment. Verbenna are exclusive and an outsider group. Hermetics are pro-science and pro-faith, Verbenna are all faith and one of the most anti science traditions out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T06:25:57-07:00","id":1447570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447406#post1447406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There can't be both?</div> </div> </div> </div>There already isn't for all intents and purposes, with Telyavs getting little more than a sidebar or couple paragraphs in a side-chapter, per edition. Outside clan novels anyhow, where they were little more than designated bad guys. The most attention they've gotten in a single edition was V20 if I remember right, and the sum total of that was a couple sub-chapters <i>and</i> a sidebar.<br /> <br /> Which is a shame for a bloodline that, in that little space, managed to pack in how they reinterpret the Pyramid, what their bloodline culture is like, and how their own interpretation of Thaumaturgy is completely different than main Tremeres', with a unique-ish discipline spread and flaw to boot.<br /> <br /> And as far as I've seen, nothing about them in V5 yet nor anything for them seemingly on the horizon. And the natural response to re-adding them is, at this point, &quot;why do it when so many resources have been dedicated to fleshing out Carna?&quot;. Carna effectively replaces the Telyavs, not compliments them, when that narrative choice wasn't <i>really</i> necessary and nu-WW could have filled that thematic gap with elements that already existed in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T06:37:21-07:00","id":1447571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447570#post1447570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as far as I've seen, nothing about them in V5 yet nor anything for them seemingly on the horizon. And the natural response to re-adding them is, at this point, &quot;why do it when so many resources have been dedicated to fleshing out Carna?&quot;. Carna effectively replaces the Telyavs, not compliments them, when that narrative choice wasn't <i>really</i> necessary and nu-WW could have filled that thematic gap with elements that already existed in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what you consider to be the &quot;point&quot; of Carna to be. Carna exists as a house because the creator of them, who we know well, was a fan of the character and interested in the idea of a group of Tremere liberating themselves from the Tremere's Blood Bond and extensive Dominate using a magical artifact.<br /> <br /> Yes, they have some overlap in the fact that Carna is a female-orientated blood mage but the Telyavs are very OLD and part of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Part of what makes Carna interesting is it's very NEW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T08:14:59-07:00","id":1447577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447571#post1447571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Carna exists as a house because the creator of them, who we know well, was a fan of the character...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically it, because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....a group of Tremere liberating themselves from the Tremere's Blood Bond and extensive Dominate using a magical artifact...but the Telyavs are very OLD and part of the Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>That's almost in its entirety what the Telyavs did. Except in the Telyavs' case it also involved a spirit that had to be either an Earthbound or Deathlord, and a roided-up Gangrel. <br /> <br /> That they're old is my point, and they're part of the Sabbat out of necessity. Even House Goratrix vampires would be more likely than not to hunt them as Tremere persecution of the Telyavs predates the schism between Camarilla and Sabbat Tremere, and their flaw and very nature of their sorcery makes them Inquisition bait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:00:32-07:00","id":1447583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447577#post1447577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's basically it, because...<br /> <br /> <br /> That's almost in its entirety what the Telyavs did. Except in the Telyavs' case it also involved a spirit that had to be either an Earthbound or Deathlord, and a roided-up Gangrel.<br /> <br /> That they're old is my point, and they're part of the Sabbat out of necessity. Even House Goratrix vampires would be more likely than not to hunt them as Tremere persecution of the Telyavs predates the schism between Camarilla and Sabbat Tremere, and their flaw and very nature of their sorcery makes them Inquisition bait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but none of which is going to have an impact on a Modern Game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:42:46-07:00","id":1447589,"title":"","content":"What would be wrong with bringing the Bahari into more prominence and giving it's members access to magic? You wouldn't have to sacrifice the Tremere then. <br /> <br /> (also, the Bahari writeup for V5 is all wrong. It's all S, when the cults were historically far more M. Stop trying to pretend you're kick-ass and give me nuance.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:49:02-07:00","id":1447590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447589#post1447589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be wrong with bringing the Bahari into more prominence and giving it's members access to magic? You wouldn't have to sacrifice the Tremere then.<br /> <br /> (also, the Bahari writeup for V5 is all wrong. It's all S, when the cults were historically far more M. Stop trying to pretend you're kick-ass and give me nuance.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused by &quot;sacrificing the Tremere&quot; as it makes no sense.<br /> <br /> There were rebel Tremere outside of the Sabbat before Carna. Hell, the Carna aren't even Anarchs in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T12:47:23-07:00","id":1447614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421860-house-carna-discussion-thread-the-good-the-bad-and-the-witchy?p=1447589#post1447589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be wrong with bringing the Bahari into more prominence and giving it's members access to magic? You wouldn't have to sacrifice the Tremere then.</div> </div> </div> </div>They kind of do. The Bahari are given two rituals that they consider to belong to them, one of which is level 5, which implies that they teach blood sorcery as a whole discipline, if not more common rituals well. I got a similar impression from the Mithraic cult, although <i>Fall of London </i>gave Mithras himself 3 dots of blood sorcery, the ancient slacker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}